---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"
import desktop from "../../../../desktop/package.json"

const wslInstall = `npm install --global --prefix "$HOME/.vector" @vectordevai/cli@${desktop.version}`

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="cli-server">

          <p>
            <code>vector serve</code> runs the agent as a headless server with <code>--port</code> and <code>--hostname</code>; <code>vector web</code> starts the same server and opens the browser interface. <code>vector attach &lt;url&gt;</code> connects a terminal session to a server that is already running, with <code>--dir</code> to choose the directory on it, the usual session flags, and <code>--username</code> and <code>--password</code> for basic auth.
          </p>
          <p class="doc-cmd"><code>vector serve --port 4096
vector attach http://localhost:4096 --dir ~/code/myapp</code><button class="doc-cmd-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy this command">Copy</button></p>
          <h3>Windows Subsystem for Linux</h3>
          <p>
            Install Linux Node.js and npm inside the WSL 2 distro before choosing Install Vector in server settings.
            The installer uses <code>{wslInstall}</code>,
            pinned to the exact version shown in About Vector, then installs a native Linux executable at
            <code>~/.vector/bin/vector-native</code>. It loads nvm and fnm when available; Node.js and npm are needed
            for installation and updates, while the installed server runs without Node.js.
            Open a terminal in that distro and run <code>VECTOR_CLI=1 ~/.vector/bin/vector-native login</code> before adding its server,
            then <code>VECTOR_CLI=1 ~/.vector/bin/vector-native auth login</code> to connect model credentials. The account token in your
            Windows app does not sign in the separate Linux installation. Existing servers that report a missing engine
            need Install Vector again. The desktop refuses mismatched versions, binds the server to Linux loopback,
            and confirms that requests without authentication are rejected before marking it ready.
          </p>
          <p>
            Server configuration uses <code>VECTOR_SERVER_PASSWORD</code> and <code>VECTOR_SERVER_USERNAME</code>;
            the default username is <code>vector</code>. The upcoming release reads only <code>VECTOR_*</code> variables;
            update server scripts and configuration before upgrading.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>vector acp</code> starts an Agent Client Protocol server, so an ACP-speaking editor can drive Vector's agent as its backend.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
